# Styling

- Colors, radius, and shadow come from semantic tokens (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`). No raw hex and no arbitrary values (`p-[13px]`).
- Conditional classes go through `cn()`. Variants go through `cva`.
- A class string used once stays on the element. Extract when the same variant set is reused.
- Responsive prefixes are mobile-first.
- Dark mode is the `.dark` token swap. Use `dark:` only when a token cannot express the override, and comment why.
- Motion uses the project duration and easing. No one-off `animate-bounce` for a status change.

Recipes: `skills/create-react-component/references/styling.md`.
